# A widget of several clauses in a static position with a dynamic parameter (Semantics
# ch. 8: the clause chosen at the build stands transparent in its caller; Type System ch.
# 1: a `$` parameter is the caller's dynamic, not a sample of it): the clause's label
# follows the caller's hold after the build. prismc once passed the clause the hold's value
# at the build, so the label never moved. Written by Claude on the claude-lowering
# branch; subject to change.
emit Ui.*
test mod Tests
use Ui.*

@Pick: fn ?Nat, $Text -> @unit
fn @Pick nil, $t:
    Ui.Label($text=$"none {$t}")                                  # 1
fn @Pick (? n), $t:
    Ui.Label($text=$"some {n} {$t}")                              # 1

@top: @unit
@top:
    !go <- Ui.Button($label=$"go")                                # 0
    $t <- "x" then "y" on !go
    @Pick (? 3), $t                                              # 1
